on't think Sam  should spend the rest of his life  serving someone else not unless he  actually wanted to do this not only is  Sam highborn but we all know Sam is a  very decent human being he's a very kind  and friendly person who could do a lot  of good for the realm Sam is a very  intelligent man and I think he deserves  to live his own life Sam's mother and  sister should still be alive too and I  believe they would accept Sam as their  Lord of Hornell Sam was already next in  line to inherit the lands but his father  forced him to join the Nights Watch so  that dick on could inherit everything  but both of them are now dead  if the Nights Watch no longer exists Sam  would no longer have to abide by the  rules but we all know Sam never followed  all of the rules anyway Sam could then  raise his family without having to worry  about his father's threats and Sam and  Gilly should move to horn Hill and start  their own family there they could even  have a child together in the future who  knows but there is one other thing Sam  could do if he would still choose to  serve in some capacity Sam could always  stay in Winterfell there is a maester  already there but Sam could take his  place if he still choose to serve we all  know that John and Sam have a very  strong bond and Sam is now creating a  relationship with bran stark and Sam and  brains relationship will blossom next  season Sam may be the only one who can  actually connect with  on some level and I think the Starks  would absolutely accept Sam into their  service if that's what he wanted to do  Sam will most likely stay by brain side  throughout season eight and depending  how things play out he may want to stay  to help bran for the rest of his life  Sam could also help deliver John and  Danny's baby if they do have a baby  together Sam said he was gonna help  deliver gillies baby and John asked him  if he knew how and Sam said he did read  about it so he could put that to use in  the future if Sam doesn't